A||||3||GodSend||Stumbling when wet||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||05-28-2001||09:41 PM||||My 87' gt has 5spd has developed a little quirk.  I recently covered the holes of the egr tube (thanks to a huge hole in it).  I havent developed a quite noticable stumble ONLY when I wash my car or its raining out.<P>To be more specific, I drive along fine for a few minutes, and then even at a constant speed the car will start to slow down (not considerably, but noticable.. like I took my foot off the gas).... a second later it will kick back in.  and everything is fine.  The frequency is random, at all speeds in all gears.  its not a cronic problem, but something I need to address.  Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-28-2001||09:44 PM||||Sounds like water is running off your rear deck lid and shorting your frt spark plug wires.  The fix would be a new set of spark plug wires, a new dist cap and rotor sounds good too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||05-28-2001||09:45 PM||||my 84 4 cylinder did the same thing, and i found out, it was cracks in the sparkplug wires.  Bought new wires and it solved the problem.<P>You can also check your distr cap if water is getting into that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GodSend||05-29-2001||12:56 AM||||Thanks guys.  The dist and rotor are pretty recent (have less then 7000 kms on them)  I did take off the cap though so I could work on the tube, perhaps its a little lose, ill have to check that.<P>Is there a way to test to see if the plug wires are cracked (should I be able to see some sparking in the dark or something?)||||reg||1
